@startuml
title State / Objects for States

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Change behavior when internal state changes; appears to change class.

**Motivation**:
Object behavior depends on state and must change at runtime.

**Applicability**:
Behavior depends on current state; complex conditional logic.

**Participants**:
Context holds State; State objects implement behavior transitions.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Removes conditionals; localizes state logic; easy to add states.
Cons: More classes; transitions may be distributed.

**Implementation Notes**:
States can be singletons; transitions occur within handle().

**Known Uses**:
UI components enabled/disabled; parsers; workflow engines.

**Related Patterns**:
Strategy (no internal transitions), Flyweight (share states), Singleton (per-state).

endlegend

class Context {
  -state : State
  +setState(s: State)
  +request()
}

interface State {
  +handle(context: Context)
}

class ConcreteStateA
class ConcreteStateB

State <|.. ConcreteStateA
State <|.. ConcreteStateB
Context o-- State
@enduml